I think society has a right and perhaps even an
obligation to quarantine those individuals
who have highly-contagious fatal or debilitating diseases.  
Drug-resistant TB comes to mind.

Does this constitute a violation of the rights of the infected?
Perhaps it does.  But there may be no reasonable alternative.   
This is one of those emergency situations where adherence to the NIOCP 
may not yield an acceptable outcome for the masses of people.


